sequenceDiagram
    %% ShiftManager Multi-Tenant Request Flow
    %% Shows how CompanyId is resolved, cached, and enforced throughout a request

    participant User as 👤 User Browser
    participant Auth as 🔐 Authentication
    participant Middleware as ⚙️ Middleware Pipeline
    participant Resolver as 🎯 TenantResolver
    participant Context as 💾 CompanyContext
    participant Page as 📄 Razor Page
    participant Service as 🔧 Service Layer
    participant Interceptor as 🛡️ CompanyIdInterceptor
    participant EF as 🗄️ EF Core + Filters
    participant DB as 💿 SQLite Database

    %% ========================================
    %% PHASE 1: Authentication & Claim Setting
    %% ========================================

    User->>Auth: POST /Login (email, password)
    Auth->>DB: Validate credentials
    DB-->>Auth: AppUser { Id=5, CompanyId=2, Role=Manager }

    Note over Auth: Create authentication cookie<br/>with claims

    Auth->>Auth: Add Claims:<br/>- NameIdentifier: "5"<br/>- CompanyId: "2"<br/>- Role: "Manager"<br/>- Email: "manager@company.com"
    Auth-->>User: Set-Cookie: .AspNetCore.Cookies=...

    Note over User,Auth: User is now authenticated<br/>CompanyId=2 stored in cookie

    %% ========================================
    %% PHASE 2: Subsequent Request with CompanyId Resolution
    %% ========================================

    User->>Middleware: GET /Schedule (with cookie)

    Note over Middleware: UseAuthentication()<br/>reads cookie, validates signature

    Middleware->>Middleware: Deserialize cookie claims<br/>User.Identity.IsAuthenticated = true

    Note over Middleware: CompanyContextMiddleware<br/>runs BEFORE page handler

    Middleware->>Resolver: GetCurrentTenantId()

    Note over Resolver: Extract CompanyId from claims

    Resolver->>Resolver: user.FindFirst("CompanyId")?<br/>Parse to int
    Resolver-->>Middleware: CompanyId = 2

    Middleware->>Context: Cache in HttpContext.Items["CurrentCompanyId"]

    Note over Context: Single lookup per request<br/>Subsequent calls use cache

    %% ========================================
    %% PHASE 3: Query Execution with Global Filters
    %% ========================================

    Middleware->>Page: Execute OnGetAsync()
    Page->>Service: GetShiftInstancesAsync(startDate, endDate)

    Service->>Resolver: GetCurrentTenantId()
    Resolver->>Context: Try get cached CompanyId
    Context-->>Resolver: CompanyId = 2 (from cache)
    Resolver-->>Service: CompanyId = 2

    Note over Service: Build query without<br/>explicit CompanyId filter

    Service->>EF: db.ShiftInstances<br/>.Where(si => si.WorkDate >= start)

    Note over EF: Global Query Filter<br/>AUTOMATICALLY injects:<br/>WHERE CompanyId = 2

    EF->>EF: Apply filter:<br/>modelBuilder.Entity&lt;ShiftInstance&gt;()<br/>.HasQueryFilter(e => e.CompanyId == resolver.GetCurrentTenantId())

    EF->>DB: SELECT * FROM ShiftInstances<br/>WHERE WorkDate >= @p0<br/>AND CompanyId = 2

    DB-->>EF: Results (only CompanyId=2 rows)
    EF-->>Service: List&lt;ShiftInstance&gt;
    Service-->>Page: Data for display
    Page-->>User: HTML response with schedule

    %% ========================================
    %% PHASE 4: Insert with CompanyIdInterceptor
    %% ========================================

    User->>Page: POST /CreateShift (form data)
    Page->>Service: CreateShiftInstanceAsync(dto)

    Service->>Resolver: GetCurrentTenantId()
    Resolver-->>Service: CompanyId = 2

    Service->>Service: Create entity:<br/>var shift = new ShiftInstance {<br/>  ShiftTypeId = 1,<br/>  WorkDate = date,<br/>  // CompanyId NOT set<br/>}

    Service->>EF: db.ShiftInstances.Add(shift)
    Service->>EF: await db.SaveChangesAsync()

    Note over EF,Interceptor: SaveChangesInterceptor<br/>runs BEFORE database write

    EF->>Interceptor: SavingChanges(context)

    Note over Interceptor: Find all Added entities<br/>implementing IBelongsToCompany

    Interceptor->>Resolver: GetCurrentTenantId()
    Resolver-->>Interceptor: CompanyId = 2

    Interceptor->>Interceptor: foreach (Added entity)<br/>if (entity.CompanyId == 0)<br/>  entity.CompanyId = 2

    Note over Interceptor: CompanyId AUTOMATICALLY<br/>set on all new entities

    Interceptor-->>EF: Continue SaveChanges

    EF->>DB: INSERT INTO ShiftInstances<br/>(ShiftTypeId, WorkDate, CompanyId)<br/>VALUES (1, '2025-06-15', 2)

    DB-->>EF: Success
    EF-->>Service: Entity saved
    Service-->>Page: Success
    Page-->>User: Redirect to /Schedule

    %% ========================================
    %% PHASE 5: Cross-Company Access (Directors)
    %% ========================================

    Note over User,DB: Special Case: Director Switching Companies

    User->>Page: POST /SwitchCompany (targetCompanyId=3)
    Page->>Service: DirectorService.IsDirectorOfAsync(3)

    Service->>DB: SELECT * FROM DirectorCompanies<br/>WHERE UserId=5 AND CompanyId=3<br/>AND IsDeleted=0

    DB-->>Service: Found (Director has access)
    Service-->>Page: true

    Page->>Resolver: SetTenantIdOverride(3)

    Note over Resolver: Override active for this request<br/>GetCurrentTenantId() returns 3

    Resolver-->>Page: Override set

    Note over Page,DB: All subsequent queries/inserts<br/>use CompanyId=3 instead of 2

    Page->>Service: GetShiftInstancesAsync(...)
    Service->>Resolver: GetCurrentTenantId()
    Resolver-->>Service: CompanyId = 3 (OVERRIDE)
    Service->>EF: db.ShiftInstances.Where(...)
    EF->>DB: WHERE CompanyId = 3
    DB-->>User: Show Company 3's schedule

    %% ========================================
    %% PHASE 6: Global Entities (OnDuty)
    %% ========================================

    Note over User,DB: Special Case: Global Entities (No CompanyId)

    User->>Page: GET /OnDuty
    Page->>Service: OnDutyService.GetOnDutiesAsync(date)

    Note over Service: OnDuty table has NO CompanyId<br/>Must use IgnoreQueryFilters()

    Service->>EF: db.OnDuties<br/>.IgnoreQueryFilters()<br/>.Where(od => od.Date == date)

    Note over EF: IgnoreQueryFilters() bypasses<br/>global query filter

    EF->>DB: SELECT * FROM OnDuties<br/>WHERE Date = @p0<br/>(NO CompanyId filter)

    DB-->>Service: All on-duty records (cross-company)
    Service-->>Page: Filtered by DirectorService permissions
    Page-->>User: Display authorized on-duty assignments

    %% ========================================
    %% SECURITY SUMMARY
    %% ========================================

    Note over User,DB: 🛡️ SECURITY GUARANTEES:<br/>✓ CompanyId stored in signed cookie (tamper-proof)<br/>✓ All queries auto-filtered by CompanyId<br/>✓ All inserts auto-set CompanyId<br/>✓ Unauthenticated users get CompanyId=0 (no data)<br/>✓ Directors explicitly authorized via DirectorCompanies table<br/>✓ Global entities require IgnoreQueryFilters() (explicit bypass)
